<title>PHILIPPINES: Two groups vie for Philippine power plant.</title>
<headline>Two groups vie for Philippine power plant.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine National Oil Co said on Thursday two groups had submitted bids to put up a 30-megawatt (mw) geothermal power plant in Mt. Apo, North Cotabato in southern Philippines.</p>
<p>First Private Power Corp submitted a bid in joint venture with Ansaldo Energia of Italy. First Private is owned by Manila Electric Co, First Philippine Holdings Corp, JG Summit Holdings Inc and PCI Capital.</p>
<p>US-based firm Oxbow Inc with Marubeni Corp of Japan also joined the bidding.</p>
<p>PNOC officials said the bidders can also opt to put up another 10-mw power plant aside from the first 30-mw.</p>
<p>The PNOC board will announce the winning bidder on October 22. Signing of the contract is scheduled on December 6.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 fax 8176267</p>
